    "narrative": "The Austin Waves roster is primed for a high-upside Friday, anchored by the elite tier of **Kyle Tucker** (78.74) and **Andy Pages** (70.49), both of whom benefit significantly from a favorable matchup against Jack Kochanowicz. With a shaky 5.12 xERA opposing them, both hitters are positioned to exploit the platoon advantage and elevated run-scoring environment. **Gunnar Henderson** (68.63) remains a foundational play despite the lack of a defined opponent, while **Miguel Vargas** (60.41) cracks the lineup with a strong efficiency score, buoyed by favorable wind conditions and a solid park factor against Andrew Painter. **Sam Antonacci** (58.45) is another intriguing volume play today; his score is propped up by a 0.379 xwOBA and wind blowing out, making him a high-efficiency beneficiary of the current weather metrics despite batting low in the order.\n\nNavigating the remainder of the lineup required difficult choices, specifically regarding the utilization of our middle infield depth. The most notable bench decision involved **Curtis Mead**, who posted a respectable 52.75 score. While **Curtis Mead** offers decent upside against Eduardo Rodriguez, he ultimately fell short of the threshold because **Nasim Nunez** (58.50) provides greater utility for our scarcity-driven strategy; even hitting ninth, **Nasim Nunez** offers the speed component that remains our priority. We are monitoring the status of **Liam Hicks** (40.50) and **Dominic Smith** (41.36), as both sit near the roster floor. Their positions are tenuous given the \"Lineup Pending\" status; if **Liam Hicks** or **Dominic Smith** are dropped to the bottom of their respective batting orders or if late scratch conditions arise, we may look to replace them with bench options like **Coby Mayo** (50.90) to preserve our game caps while maintaining production.",
